hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24355","Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sa'd al-Ansari narrated to us, who said: I heard Abu Zabyah al-Kala'i saying: I heard al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to his Companions: What do you say about adultery, they said: Allah and His Messenger have forbidden it, so it is forbidden until the Day of Resurrection, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to his Companions: For a man to commit adultery with ten women is lighter for him than to commit adultery with his neighbor's wife, then he said: What do you say about theft, they said: Allah and His Messenger have forbidden it, so it is forbidden, he said: For a man to steal from ten houses is lighter for him than to steal from his neighbor."
